// The morphogen package: form that arises from growth rules
// (morphogenesis), made as graphs of points. A program reaches it with
// 'import morphogen', and gets:
//
// - Branch graphs (graph.cone): 'BranchGraph', a forest of nodes, each a
//   point with its parent (a root has none), the step it grew in and a
//   radius; 'pipeRadii', each node's radius by the pipe model (Shinozaki
//   et al. 1964: a branch's radius to the power 'exponent' is the sum of
//   its children's, the tips given one radius); 'smoothBranches', the
//   kinks of growth taken out of each strand; 'pruneTwigs', the short
//   twigs a growth leaves taken off; 'strands', the graph cut into paths
//   (from a root or a fork along the child carrying the most to a tip),
//   each to be drawn as one tube or chain.
// - Space colonization (colonize.cone): 'Growth', the dials (step, the
//   reach of the attraction and the distance that consumes an attractor,
//   tropism, inertia, seeded jitter); 'colonize', a graph grown from its
//   roots into a cloud of attraction points (Runions, Lane and
//   Prusinkiewicz, "Modeling trees with a space colonization algorithm",
//   2007); 'scatter', a seeded cloud of points in a box.
// - Capsules (capsules.cone): 'CapsuleSet', tapered capsules in chains (a
//   strand's segments) and the grid of buckets that finds them, in Lists
//   it owns, lent as an sdf.Capsules view, the field that fuses them.
//
// The graph is the skeleton of a tree, a root system, veins, lightning or
// a vine; what it is made into is the caller's choice: tapered capsules
// smooth-unioned (a CapsuleSet, viewed as sdf's Capsules), or a tube swept
// along each strand (sculpt's sweep). Nothing here draws or meshes.
//
// DETERMINISTIC. Every random choice is an integer hash of the seed and an
// index (noise's PCG hashes), every loop runs in index order, and nothing
// depends on addresses or timing: the same dials give the same bits every
// run. Children are always numbered after their parents, which the
// functions that walk the graph rely on.
//
// Its files are one module, and only this one, the root, imports:
//
//   graph.cone      BranchGraph, Strands, pipeRadii, smoothBranches, pruneTwigs
//   colonize.cone   Growth, colonize, scatter
//   capsules.cone   CapsuleSet

mod morphogen;

import libc;
import geomath use *;
import collections use *;
import noise;
import sdf;
